# Launching the Dev Server

This project doesn't have `http-server` installed as a local dependency, so `npx http-server` can hang while downloading.

## Reliable method (Python — always available on macOS)

```bash
cd public && python3 -m http.server 8081
```

Then open http://localhost:8081 in the browser:

```bash
open http://localhost:8081
```

## When the user says "push to browser", "open the app", or "let me see it"

1. Check if anything is already running on port 8081: `lsof -i :8081`
2. If not, start the Python server in the `public/` folder (background it so the terminal stays usable).
3. Open the browser with `open http://localhost:8081`.

## Stopping the server

Kill the process on port 8081:

```bash
lsof -ti :8081 | xargs kill
```
